error[E-plus-minus]: `+-` means `+ (-…)` in Rust
   --> cascades.spl:12:51
   |
12 |     let r2 = Resistor { a: vcc, b: gnd, value: 1k +- 1% };
   |                                                   ^^ not a tolerance
   |
   = help: for a tolerance write `±` or `+/-`

error[E-chained]: tolerances can't be chained
   --> cascades.spl:13:56
   |
13 |     let r3 = Resistor { a: vcc, b: gnd, value: 1k ± 1% ± 1% };
   |                                                        ^ second operator here

error[E-ambiguous-tolerance]: ambiguous tolerance
   --> cascades.spl:14:48
   |
14 |     let r4 = Resistor { a: vcc, b: gnd, value: 1k / 2 ± 10% };
   |                                                ^^^^^^ does `±` apply to this whole expression?
   |
   = help: `(1k / 2) ± 10%` for a spread on the result
   = help: `1k / (2 ± 10%)` for a spread on one term

error[E-spread]: a range endpoint can't carry a tolerance
   --> cascades.spl:15:50
   |
15 |     let q1 = Npn { c: vcc, b: gnd, e: gnd, beta: 100 ± 1% ..= 300 };
   |                                                  ^^^^^^^^ this endpoint has a tolerance
   |
   = help: use either a range `a..=b` or a tolerance `x ± t`
